{"description":"Validate progressive disclosure trade-off (H4, Finding 2/3): does L2 (dependency --no-content, refs) + lazy expand on explicit role==constraint/depends-on beat single upfront full context (all neighbor content) on tokens, turns, task success, and p50 latency. Decides whether the proposed L2-default + expand guardrail should become the canonical agent instruction.","investigationNotes":"Context: Finding 2 maps L0-L6 to existing primitives (--no-content/--compact/depth) and claims single L2 covers \u003e70% of tasks without expansion; Finding 3 declares Context Object is the package (refs vs full docs). Claim is HYPOTHESIS — net win depends on extra retrieval turns cost.\n\nExperiment E3 (H4): Variant A = one upfront dependency full (all neighbor content); Variant B = L2 --no-content then agent may expand 0-2 neighbors (capped at 2 fetches, guardrail: if constraints non-empty at L2, expand minimal constraint set). Same tasks as E1 (fix/implement/review, 10-15 tasks). Metrics: tokens_transmitted, turns, task success rubric, p50 latency wall-clock, expansion rate (how many tasks needed 0/1/2 fetches).\n\nAlso measure failure mode: premature stop at L2 when constraint needed → hallucinated contradiction. Needs real eka context + eka get calls, no mock. Timebox 3 days. Output: recommendation for skill pack wording ('Always start L2, fetch focus.content via eka get \u003clineForm\u003e only when implementing, fetch neighbor content on role==constraint') either VALIDATED or REVISED (e.g., single-shot better for one-shot tasks).","conclusion":""}